Deliberately not an open-source licence, for the same reason as the author's
other projects: this was built as a side project with the intention that it
might eventually earn money, and a permissive licence would let anyone stand up
a competing service from the same code. If that stops being the goal, MIT is a
one-file change.

This notice covers the code. It does not cover the data in docs/data/, which is
generated from files the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services publishes in
its Provider Data Catalog (data.cms.gov), including its archive of past monthly
editions. Those facts belong to CMS's public record rather than to this project,
and nothing in this notice grants or restricts rights over them. The data files
are included because the page in docs/ is static and reads them directly.
